      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://hackaday.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/computersaretakingover.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🔧 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhackaday.com%2F2026%2F10%2F27%2Fsimd-accelerated-machine-vision-on-an-esp32-s3%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<div><img alt=\"\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" height=\"251\" src=\"https://hackaday.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/computersaretakingover.jpg?w=800\" style=\"margin:0 auto;margin-bottom:15px;\" width=\"800\"/></div>Recently [shraiwi] decided to have a bit of good nerdy fun and implement the FAST machine vision algorithm on an ESP32-S3 using its SIMD ISA. This involves using the assembly <a class=\"read-more\" href=\"https://hackaday.com/2026/10/27/simd-accelerated-machine-vision-on-an-esp32-s3/\">…read more</a>",
