      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/makezine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/omnibot-ringo-hero.jpg?fit=1360%2C768&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🔧 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmakezine.com%2Farticle%2Ftechnology%2Frobotics%2Fomnibot-reborn-giving-a-1984-robot-butler-the-brain-it-was-promised%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<div><img alt=\"Tomy Omnibot with Ring-O companion robot mounted on an arm, OLED eye glowing\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium wp-post-image\" height=\"424\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/makezine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/omnibot-ringo-hero.jpg?fit=750%2C424&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"margin-bottom:15px;\" width=\"750\"/></div>\n<p>In 1984, Tomy sold a toy robot that promised a domestic future it couldn’t quite deliver. Forty years later, a maker in Miami gave it vision, a voice, and just enough intelligence to finally pull it off.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://makezine.com/article/technology/robotics/omnibot-reborn-giving-a-1984-robot-butler-the-brain-it-was-promised/\">Omnibot Reborn: Giving a 1984 Robot Butler the Brain It Was Promised</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://makezine.com\">Make: DIY Projects and Ideas for Makers</a>.</p>",
